        {
          "type": "kotak",
          "title": "Чоловік: one word, two meanings",
          "items": [
            "**Чоловік** means both \"husband\" **and** \"man\". *Мій чоловік* = my husband; *цей чоловік* = that man. Context decides, and Ukrainians are never confused.",
            "Its partner, **жінка**, also works both ways: \"wife\" and \"woman\". For \"wife\", the warmer and more common word is **дружина** (originally \"companion\").",
            "⚠️ Don't translate \"man\" as *мужчина* — that's a Russian word. The Ukrainian form is **чоловік**."
          ]
        },
